</div>
<details id="speechMore" class="speech-more"><summary>More filters & assumptions</summary>
<div class="controls speech-advanced"><select id="speechAccess" aria-label="Speech model access"><option value="all">All models</option><option value="open">Open weights</option><option value="closed">Closed / hosted</option><option value="unknown">Unknown access</option><option value="unreleased">Unreleased weights</option></select><select id="speechSize" aria-label="Reported download size"><option value="">All download sizes</option><option value="200">Download ≤200 MB</option><option value="500">Download ≤500 MB</option><option value="1000">Download ≤1,000 MB</option></select><select id="speechParams" aria-label="Reported parameter count"><option value="">All parameter counts</option><option value="100">Parameters ≤100 M</option><option value="500">Parameters ≤500 M</option><option value="1000">Parameters ≤1,000 M</option></select></div>
<label class="estimate-rate">Illustrative local compute: $<input id="speechHourlyRate" type="number" min="0.01" max="1000" step="0.01" value="1" aria-label="Assumed device cost in USD per hour"> / device-hour · 100% utilization, not a market quote</label>
<section class="history-bar" data-release-start="{{ stt.config.release_start }}" data-snapshot-date="{{ stt.config.snapshot_date }}" aria-label="Historical speech model release cutoff">
<div class="hist-head"><span>Model cutoff <strong id="historyDate">{{ stt.config.snapshot_date }}</strong></span><button type="button" class="quiet" id="historyLatest">Latest</button></div>
<input type="range" id="historyRange" min="0" max="365" step="1" value="365" aria-label="Speech model release date cutoff">
<div class="axis"><span id="rangeStart">{{ stt.config.release_start }}</span><span id="rangeEnd">{{ stt.config.snapshot_date }}</span></div><small id="historyStatus">Unknown availability dates appear only in the current view. API rates retain their pricing dates.</small>
</section>
<p class="key" id="speechProtocolNote">The same seven English test sets, averaged equally. Sizes do not affect accuracy rank.</p>


</details>
<div class="speech-summary"><p class="key" id="speechStatus" role="status">{{ stt.protocolInitial.benchmarkCount }} ranked · best accuracy first · {{ stt.protocolInitial.speedCount }} speed scenarios · {{ stt.protocolInitial.priceCount }} API rates · {{ stt.protocolInitial.localCostCount }} local estimates</p><button type="button" class="quiet" id="speechReset">Reset</button></div>
<p class="speech-context" id="speechSpeedNote">Speed: M4 Max Q8 deployment spans. Cost: API rates or estimated local compute at $1/device-hour, fully utilized.</p>
<section id="speechMatrixPanel" aria-label="Speech accuracy leaderboard">
<div class="table-scroll"><table id="speechTable" class="speech-table compact"><thead><tr id="speechHead">{{ stt.protocolInitial | speechHead | safe }}</tr></thead><tbody id="speechBody">{{ stt.protocolInitial | speechRows(stt) | safe }}</tbody></table></div>
<details id="speechUnscored" class="comparison-note"><summary id="speechUnscoredSummary">{{ stt.protocolInitial.unscoredRows.length }} configurations without a matched accuracy score</summary><p>No complete, comparable result for this benchmark. These models are not scored as worse; other benchmarks may be available.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table class="speech-table compact"><thead><tr id="speechUnscoredHead">{{ stt.protocolInitial | speechHead | safe }}</tr></thead><tbody id="speechUnscoredList">{{ stt.protocolInitial | speechUnscored(stt) | safe }}</tbody></table></div></details>
<p class="key speech-legend">WER / OI-WER = word-error metrics · × = realtime throughput, higher is faster · ≈ / est. = assumed deployment or compute scenario · — = unsupported / unavailable</p>
<noscript><p>The English accuracy ranking and source documentation are available without JavaScript. JavaScript enables release replay, detailed protocol views and filters.</p></noscript>
</section>
<details class="method" id="methodology"><summary>Methodology, provenance & sources</summary>
<p>This is an index of published speech recognition evidence. We have not executed the transcription models. WER is 100 × (substitutions + deletions + insertions) / reference words, so it can exceed 100%. Punctuation, diarization, hallucinations and latency need their own measurements.</p>
<p>Each accuracy selection uses one fixed protocol: a complete matched panel or one named dataset. Ranks are calculated before search and filters. Different datasets and speed hardware must not be compared as one quality score.</p>

<p>The default is English accuracy: ascending unrounded seven-set mean WER, with tied results sharing a rank. Download sizes and parameter counts are metadata, not ranking weights. Missing scores appear separately without a numeric rank. This English-focused order is not a universal multilingual, long-form or streaming ranking.</p>
<p>The benchmark selector contains both complete panels and individual datasets/languages. Partial evidence stays available without inventing an overall score. Historical aggregate indices remain in the source data, but are not used to order this table.</p>
<p>Sources may be vendor, competitor, community, or maintainer publications, not independent reproductions. Row Details preserves execution attribution, source qualifications, size metadata, rates and other reported speed measurements.</p>
<p>The release slider uses verified availability dates, not paper publication, result dates or Hub repository creation. Unknown releases appear only in the current view. Quantized runtime conversions have separate identities and do not inherit upstream release dates, scores, size or memory use. Catalog confidence intervals and sample counts remain in the downloadable data. Legacy-published catalog cells can lack a run date or engine SHA.</p>
<p>Source preference within a matched protocol is maintainer publication, independent third party, community, model author, then vendor/secondary evidence. Alternative observations are preserved; conflicts are not averaged. Assumed, incompatible and private/vendor-internal values cannot supply core coverage, maturity or index. FFASR’s private corpus is not assigned a core vote. The original Phonon-2 164 MB package and its approximately 740 MB GGUF Q8_0 artifact are different configurations.</p>
<p>Model sizes are checked separately from accuracy results. Downloads refer to the linked weight artifact and its precision, not runtime RAM or a full software installation. Parameters may be author-reported architecture counts or Hub stored-tensor counts; source notes distinguish them. Missing values remain — when no matching public artifact or count is verified, including hosted services and unverified runtime variants. Downloads and parameters are rounded only for display; filters and sorting use the recorded precision.</p>
<p>Deployment estimates use only exact upstream Hub identity links to measured Q8 conversions, not parameter-count speed extrapolation or hardware normalization. The two short-clip speed range is not a confidence interval. Quantization may change accuracy; the original accuracy score is never copied to the deployment proxy. Speed sorting uses the lower throughput in the span; cost sorting uses the higher cost, at the chosen illustrative device-hour rate and 100% utilization. Overlapping ranges do not establish a reliable winner. API tariffs remain separate measured-source rates, not model-size estimates.</p>
<p>Memory labels show the assumed FP16 weight-only floor from total parameters, not full VRAM requirements. Runtime memory is additional; batch, audio length, attention, decoder caches and implementation matter. M4 uses unified RAM rather than dedicated VRAM. Exact supported Whisper models include separate <a href="https://github.com/openai/whisper#available-models-and-languages">OpenAI PyTorch planning guidance</a> in Details; it is not the Q8 speed configuration. <a href="https://github.com/handy-computer/transcribe.cpp/blob/main/docs/input-limits.md">Runtime input-limit documentation</a>.</p>
<p>Further gaps include matched diarization and silence/hallucination tests, broader independently verified release dates, and comparable streaming p50/p95 latency and peak RAM. The latency paper and tiny runtime speed clips do not supply these missing measurements.</p>
<p><a href="/stt/data.json">Download the source data JSON</a> · {{ stt.counts.sources }} documented sources. Prices retain their own as-of dates in historical model views.</p>
<div class="source-grid">{% for id, source in stt.sources %}<p id="source-{{ id }}"><a href="{{ source.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">{{ source.title }}</a><br><small>Publication: {{ source.publication_operator }} · execution: {{ source.measurement_operator }} · checked {{ source.verified_on }}. {{ source.note }}</small></p>{% endfor %}</div>
</details>
<footer>Evidence checked {{ stt.config.snapshot_date }} · {{ stt.counts.models }} configurations · <a href="/ocr/">OCR evidence benchmark</a></footer>
</main><script src="{{ "/assets/js/ranking.js" | assetUrl }}"></script><script src="{{ "/assets/js/rank-ui.js" | assetUrl }}"></script><script src="{{ "/assets/js/speech-estimates.js" | assetUrl }}"></script><script src="{{ "/assets/js/speech.js" | assetUrl }}"></script><script src="{{ "/assets/js/speech-page.js" | assetUrl }}"></script></body></html>
